From 7ba263d1f419fbd5884bed0b7064b15eed23964c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:16:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kokkos initialized by mfem_mgis::initialize on demand
 (enable-kokkos)

The behaviours generated by the kokkos backend of the generic-parallel
interface of MFront require an initialized Kokkos, which they do not
initialize ("Kokkos is not initialized"). With the CMake option
enable-kokkos (OFF by default), mfem_mgis::initialize initializes Kokkos
if the option --kokkos (or -kk, declared by declareDefaultOptions) is
given, or else if the environment variable MFEM_MGIS_KOKKOS is set to a
non empty value other than 0, after the device of MFEM and on its GPU;
mfem_mgis::finalize finalizes it before MPI if it initialized it.
Without enable-kokkos, the option is an error and the variable is
ignored with a warning, as the one of the pool of memory of hypre.
isKokkosInitialized gives the state of Kokkos.

The only source including Kokkos (src/KokkosRuntime.cxx) is compiled by
the compiler of Kokkos in the shared library MFEMMGISKokkos, privately
linked to Kokkos::kokkos, installed and exported with MFEMMGIS (symbols
exported despite -fvisibility=hidden, run path to the libraries of
Kokkos). The other sources of mfem-mgis and the projects linked to it
thus inherit neither the flags of Kokkos nor its launcher: a static
MFEMMGIS linked to Kokkos::kokkos would pass the link options of Kokkos
(-DKOKKOS_DEPENDENCE -arch=sm_XX) to every program, which then fails to
link outside the launcher of Kokkos, for instance in
check_cxx_source_compiles. The installed configuration does not search
Kokkos.

Tests: KokkosOptionTest (option, short option, variable, variable set to
0 or overridden by --no-kokkos; Kokkos initialized and finalized as
expected, or the option refused without Kokkos; the tests initializing a
Kokkos built for a GPU require the GPU tests);
MaterialArraysTest-kokkos, the point-wise model generated by the kokkos
backend being integrated on the GPU. The installation guide and the
guide of the computations by batches describe the option, its
requirements, and the backends of the generic-parallel interface which
run in mfem-mgis.
